Two stars A and B have their surfaces separated by a distance of $1.4 \times 10^{12}\,\mathrm{m}$, as illustrated in Fig. 1.1.

{{figure:figure_1_1.png}}

Point P lies on the line joining the centres of the two stars. The distance $x$ of point P from the surface of star A may be varied.

The variation with distance $x$ of the gravitational potential $\phi$ at point P is shown in Fig. 1.2.

{{figure:figure_1_2.png}}

A rock of mass $180\,\mathrm{kg}$ moves along the line joining the centres of the two stars, from star A towards star B.
